SmartSessionEmissary::verifyExecution
├── given USE mode
│   ├── given single call execution
│   │   ├── it returns verifyExecution selector
│   │   └── when session validator rejects signature
│   │       └── it returns INVALID_SIGNATURE
│   ├── given batch call execution
│   │   ├── it returns verifyExecution selector
│   │   └── when one action in batch is not enabled
│   │       └── it reverts
│   ├── given cache behavior
│   │   ├── it caches digest after successful validation
│   │   ├── it returns success from cache on second call
│   │   ├── it isolates cache per account
│   │   └── it isolates cache per permissionId
│   ├── when caller is not intent executor
│   │   └── it reverts with UnauthorizedSource
│   ├── when permissionId is invalid
│   │   └── it reverts with InvalidPermissionId
│   ├── when action selector is not enabled
│   │   └── it reverts
│   ├── when target is not enabled
│   │   └── it reverts
│   ├── when emissary data is empty
│   │   └── it reverts
│   └── given isolation
│       ├── it isolates action policies per account
│       ├── it isolates action policies per permissionId
│       ├── it isolates action policies per actionId
│       └── it isolates action policies per target
├── given ENABLE mode
│   ├── it enables session and returns verifyExecution selector
│   ├── when enable data is expired
│   │   └── it reverts with InvalidEmissaryEnableData
│   ├── when permissionId does not match config
│   │   └── it reverts with InvalidPermissionId
│   ├── when user signature is invalid
│   │   └── it reverts with InvalidUserSignature
│   ├── given re-enable (session already enabled)
│   │   ├── when first enable was via setConfig
│   │   │   ├── when allocator signature is valid
│   │   │   │   └── it returns verifyExecution selector
│   │   │   └── when allocator signature is invalid
│   │   │       └── it reverts with InvalidAllocatorSignature
│   │   └── when first enable was via verifyExecution ENABLE mode
│   │       ├── when nonce is fresh (rebuilt after first enable)
│   │       │   └── it returns verifyExecution selector
│   │       └── when nonce is stale (not rebuilt after first enable)
│   │           └── it reverts with HashMismatch
│   └── given NO_LOCKTAG flow
│       └── it enables session without allocator signature
└── given unsupported mode (UNSAFE_ENABLE)
    └── it reverts with UnsupportedSmartSessionMode